  "slug": "agentic-operation-harness-54b9",
  "summary": "Open tools now pair whole-slide, browser-based and cloud quantification with explicit numerical verification against reference implementations.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is making bioimaging and quantitative image analysis available as open, accessible tooling rather than bespoke scripts. StainAI-Web offers a cloud server for automated whole-slide microglial morphology detection in IHC sections, with ROI-based regional quantification. WispLab provides open-source browser workbenches for Western blot, histology and qPCR quantification, each checked numerically against separate Python reference implementations. OpenDVP packages MCMICRO, QuPath and napari with scverse AnnData and SpatialData into an end-to-end framework for deep visual proteomics. The items do not share a single modality, so the thread is one of delivery rather than shared biology. What is new is the pairing of whole-slide throughput with browser- or cloud-based access and explicit reference-based verification. The summaries do not report comparative benchmarks against existing tools, so performance relative to alternatives is unreported here.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-23"
}
